# Tessera stdlib: the correctly rounded gamma function of B64
#
# A double-double fast phase with an error bound: a polynomial for 1/gamma
# near zero, a polynomial around 3.5 + i shifted by the recurrence for
# -3 <= x <= 4, exp(lgamma(x)) from Stirling's series above 4, and the
# reflection formula below -3. When the bound can't decide the rounding, an
# accurate phase redoes it with a triple-double product of powers of the
# reduced argument over nine ranges, and a table settles the hardest inputs.
# Round to nearest only: overflow gives +inf, +-0 gives +-inf, the negative
# integers and -inf give NaN, a result below the subnormals rounds to a zero
# with the true sign, and NaN comes back quiet.
#
# This file also holds the double-double helpers and the logarithm shared with
# the log-gamma port (Lgamma.te).
#
# Ported from CORE-MATH, src/binary64/tgamma/tgamma.c via RazorForge's B64Tgamma.rf.
# Copyright (c) 2024 Alexei Sibidanov <sibid@uvic.ca>
# MIT license: see LICENSE-CORE-MATH

module Standard/Core

